			"image": "/images/AvbcKI1lJe9DQAxd9cp9ERMpmrQ.avif",
			"title": "Building a Photography Portfolio with Presence",
			"excerpt": "A strong photography portfolio does more than collect images. It gives your point of view a clear shape and helps the right clients understand what you see.",
			"author": {
				"name": "Hreka",
				"role": "Photographer & Visual Artist",
				"avatar": "/images/about.webp"
			},
			"date": "Aug 14, 2024",
			"isoDate": "2024-08-14",
			"content": "<p>A strong photography portfolio does more than collect images. It gives your point of view a clear shape and helps the right clients understand what you see.</p><p>Choose work that feels connected by your way of seeing, not only by the subject. A clear edit makes the portfolio easier to remember and easier to trust.</p>"
		},
		{
			"id": 2,
			"image": "/images/2P7bB8uwsuqvnasZuwSMEzKDWb8.avif",
			"title": "How to Prepare for a Brand Photoshoot",
			"excerpt": "A practical guide to aligning your concept, shot list, location, and team before the camera comes out.",
			"date": "Mar 15, 2022",
			"isoDate": "2022-03-15",
			"content": "<p>A successful brand photoshoot begins before the first frame. Start with a clear purpose, a focused reference board, and a shot list that supports the story.</p>"
		},
		{
			"id": 3,
			"image": "/images/jAvdkVwcxN6xtJDoAVnlmrTEjA.avif",
			"title": "Finding the Right Light for a Portrait",
			"excerpt": "Explore how direction, softness, and timing can change the feeling of a portrait before you change anything else.",
			"date": "Apr 8, 2022",
			"isoDate": "2022-04-08",
			"content": "<p>Great portraits begin with attention. Direction, window light, and enough time for a subject to settle can create more honesty than complicated equipment.</p>"
		},
		{
			"id": 4,
			"image": "/images/lR2uF17C7oB3HnOxQe6JE2i19k.avif",
			"title": "Why Visual Consistency Matters for Brands",
			"excerpt": "Learn how a consistent image language helps a brand feel recognizable, considered, and trustworthy.",
			"date": "Jun 12, 2024",
			"isoDate": "2024-06-12",
			"content": "<p>Visual consistency helps people recognize a brand before they read a word. Repeated choices in light, color, framing, and texture build that recognition.</p>"
		},
		{
			"id": 5,
			"image": "/images/project5.avif",
			"title": "The Details That Make an Image Feel Real",
			"excerpt": "A closer look at texture, gesture, imperfection, and the small decisions that give photographs their character.",
			"date": "Jan 7, 2023",
			"isoDate": "2023-01-07",
			"content": "<p>The smallest details often carry the most feeling: a hand in motion, a worn surface, a pause between expressions. Look closely and let those details guide the frame.</p>"
